Creating an object
2 steps
	Declaring a reference variable the class type
	Assigning the variables with an explicitly allocated instance of the class type

"new" operator
	explicitly allocates adn object of the specified class type

Example:
	Restaurant favLunchPlace = new Restaurant();

	creates a Restaurant object named faveLunchPlace

"." operator
	member access operator
	invokes a method on an object
	
	Example:
	favLunchPlace.setRating(4);
		calls the method setRating on the object favLunchPlace, passes 4 to the method

Example:

public class RestaurantFavorites {
   public static void main(String[] args) {
      Restaurant favLunchPlace = new Restaurant();
      Restaurant favDinnerPlace = new Restaurant();

      favLunchPlace.setName("Central Deli");
      favLunchPlace.setRating(4);

      favDinnerPlace.setName("Friends Cafe");
      favDinnerPlace.setRating(5);

      System.out.println("My favorite restaurants: ");
      favLunchPlace.print();
      favDinnerPlace.print();
   }
}

