Mutators, accessors, private helpers

Mutator
	Able to modify (mutate) a class' fields

Accessor
	Able to acces fields, but cannot modify a class' fields

2 assocaited methods
	mutator -> setting a value
		setter
	accessor -> getting a value
		getter

Setter and Getter methods

Methods typically start with "set" or "get"

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Example

Restaurant.java

public class Restaurant {                          
   private String name;
   private int rating;

   public void setName(String restaurantName) {  // Mutator
      name = restaurantName;
   }

   public void setRating(int userRating) {       // Mutator
      rating = userRating;
   }

   public String getName() {  // Accessor
      return name;
   }

   public int getRating() {  // Accessor
      return rating;
   }

   public void print() {      // Accessor
      System.out.println(name + " -- " + rating);
   }
}

